@startuml
' Derived from src/nonogram/difficulty.py:316 (TIER_BANDS), :342 (RUNG_BANDS),
' :200-226 (the four constants) and :464 (classify).
' The two tables are deliberately NOT derived from each other (difficulty.py:342).
title The two band tables — a rung boundary re-scales, a tier cutoff re-files

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "0..100 score scale (SCORE_MIN=0.0, SCORE_MAX=100.0)" {

  rectangle "RUNG_BANDS — what score_difficulty reads\n(moving one of these RE-SCALES every score)" as R {
    rectangle "simple_overlap\n[0, 33]" as R1 #E8F4E8
    rectangle "line_dp\n(33, 66]" as R2 #FFF4D6
    rectangle "probe_contradiction\n(66, 100]" as R3 #FFE0E0
    R1 -[hidden]right- R2
    R2 -[hidden]right- R3
  }

  rectangle "TIER_BANDS — what classify() reads\n(moving one of these RE-FILES scores that do not change)" as T {
    rectangle "Tier.EASY\n[0, 33]" as T1 #E8F4E8
    rectangle "Tier.MEDIUM\n(33, 90]\n= all of line_dp + the lower 70.6%\nof probe_contradiction" as T2 #FFF4D6
    rectangle "Tier.HARD\n(90, 100]" as T3 #FFE0E0
    T1 -[hidden]right- T2
    T2 -[hidden]right- T3
  }
}

R -[hidden]down- T

note bottom of R
  RUNG_OVERLAP_MAX_SCORE = 33.0
  RUNG_LINE_DP_MAX_SCORE  = 66.0

  score = band_low(rung) + share * band_width(rung)
  rung  = the hardest rung that settled >= 1 cell
  share = rung_cells[rung] / total_cells

  Monotonicity is STRUCTURAL: share <= 1 so a rung
  cannot pass its band's top, and a present rung has
  share > 0 so it cannot reach its band's floor.
end note

note bottom of T
  EASY_MAX_SCORE   = 33.0  (unchanged since ADR-0005)
  MEDIUM_MAX_SCORE = 90.0  (66.0 -> 90.0, owner's decision
                            2026-09-23, CARD-137)

  33.0 still coincides with the top rung band, so
  Easy means EXACTLY "the overlap rule finished it".

  90.0 coincides with NOTHING on the ladder. At 66.0 it
  did, and Medium then meant "topped out at line_dp" —
  measured at 5 puzzles in 300 on production.

  No stored grade moved: RUNG_BANDS was not touched.
end note

note right of R3
  `guess` is NOT on this ladder.
  A branching solve is reported as the
  `guess` STRATEGY (solver.STRATEGY_GUESS),
  appended exactly once, in
  orchestrator.Puzzle.record_difficulty.

  ADR-0025's Tier.GUESS was retired on
  evidence: 0 assignments of 6,620, of 462,
  and of 16 stored rows.
end note

@enduml
